  "version": 2,
  "mini_caption": "Figure 1. The finite-difference trap. Large \u03b5 (orange) mis-signs the gradient \u2014 the secant straddles a feature (each probe carries its own setpoint draw, r = 0.02). Shrinking \u03b5 does not help: at \u03b5 = \u221a2\u00b7r = 0.028 the setpoint error alone makes the one-sigma slope error equal to |\u2207C| (purple cone), and even the best step \u03b5* = 0.11 leaves an RMSE of 28% of |\u2207C| (B.6.4; Sec. 6.2). The shift-rule tangent (PSR/NSR, blue) recovers \u2207C_device with no step size to tune.",
  "data_note": "DATA NOTE (Fig 1): H(\u03b8)=\u03b8\u00b7Z0+X0, C_device=\u27e8Z0\u27e9 under T2* dephasing, Hamiltonian-level (setpoint draw r=0.02 on every probe, P0-0; B.6.4 at the anchor: f2=-2.18, f3=+1645, eps*=0.108, floor 32% of |f1| vs shot-free MC best eps=0.108 at 28%; cone at eps=sqrt2\u00b7r=0.028, wrong sign 15%; drawn secants carry seed-0 draws, wrong-signed in [97, 100, 100]% of draws; eps labels in the paper's \u03b8\u00b1\u03b5/2 convention). R8 grid sweep over T\u00d7\u03b8*\u00d7\u03b5_min (T/T2*=0.5 fixed) \u2192 41 configs pass; chosen NON-MARGINAL (R9): T=12 (T2=24), \u03b8*=1.290, \u03b5=[0.18, 0.25, 0.32]. Criteria: (1) secant slopes +0.70/+1.39/+0.53 \u2014 all wrong-signed vs \u2207C_device=-4.35, min|slope|=0.53\u22650.15 \u2713; (2) anchor 0.077 from nearest extremum = 25% of period 0.313 \u226520% \u2713 (margin); (3) |slope| 4.35 = 61% of max|slope| 7.13 \u226550% \u2713; (4) no collisions \u2713. Drawn tangent slope = analytic \u2207C_device = -4.347 (h=1e-3), EQUAL by construction; np.gradient check -4.35. SMALL-\u03b5 (R10): \u03b5 floored by \u03b4=0.02 (Q1-pending \u2014 cone geometry depends on \u03b4; re-render if \u03b4 changes). Cone drawn at \u03b5=0.03\u2248\u03b4 (1.5\u00d7\u03b4; labelled \u03b5\u2248\u03b4): mean -4.01 vs true -4.35, std 1.66, 3% wrong-signed. \u03b5-window sweep over [\u03b4,\u03bb/2=0.16] @N=4000: best \u03b5=0.056 (RMSE/|g|=0.28); usable window [0.026,0.072] (width 0.047, ~34% of [\u03b4,\u03bb/2]). USABLE-WINDOW CRITERION (shared with F6, G2/F8): an \u03b5 is 'usable' iff RMSE/|\u2207C_device| < 0.5 AND sign-error < 5% \u2014 the window is the \u03b5-range meeting BOTH (NOT the interval [\u03b4,\u03bb/2], which is only the swept range / the fraction's denominator). HONESTY: FD is NOT trapped from below at this anchor \u2014 a usable \u03b5 exists; Fig 1 asserts only that the shift rules need no \u03b5 (safe), and defers FD's quantitative defeat to Sec 6.2/F6-R."
